        "abstract": "The request for high-throughput NAND Flash memory systems for applications such as smart phones, tablets, and laptop PCs with solid-state drives (SSDs) is largely increasing. At the same time, NAND systems must meet strictly maximum power specifications. The power limit also changes depending on the specific application: for enterprise environments and for mobile solutions can be hugely different. Only the systems that have effective and adaptative power management architectures on board can guarantee the performance required by the market complying the max power limit. This paper describes the state of the art of power management architectures, discusses the open challenges in the field and outlines new solutions for the next generations of high-performance NAND systems.",
